<!--
  The launcher's monochrome rabbit, scaled up to fill a notification icon.

  A notification small icon is drawn as a **silhouette**: Android throws away every colour in it and
  tints the non-transparent pixels, which is why this reuses the monochrome layer's path rather than
  the full-colour launcher art. The path itself is generated — regenerate it in
  art/make-launcher-icon.py, don't hand-edit it here.

  The scale exists because the adaptive-icon path is drawn inside a 108x108 viewport with a large
  safe zone around it, and dropped into a 24dp notification slot unchanged the rabbit would be a
  speck. The art's bounding box is already centred on (54, 54), so the group needs a scale and no
  translation.
-->
